    "attribute": "arrangement",
    "likely_right_file": "bhel/Part1.pdf",
    "likely_right_page": 44,
    "why": "Both Part1.pdf and Part4.pdf explicitly specify a 1W+1S (one working, one standby) arrangement, whereas 2X100% in Part3.pdf denotes the same physical capacity (two 100% duty pumps) without explicitly assigning working and standby roles. The 1W+1S notation is clearer and matches the terminology of the proposed change.",
    "consequence": "Because 1W+1S and 2X100% normally mean the same physical pump sizing, there is low physical risk unless 2X100% is misinterpreted during the upgrade as two simultaneously running pumps, which would result in double the required flow rate, oversized discharge piping, or overloaded electrical supply."
   }
